{"description":"Bare `eka get ses:execution-state` resolves through the default resolver namespace and returns `eka/ses:execution-state`, even when invoked inside another project. `cmd/get.go` passes the bare target directly to `Resolver.Resolve` without current repository ProjectID or namespace context.","impact":"CLI users and planning agents receive unrelated execution state, violating per-project/per-repo isolation and making execution context untrustworthy.","acceptanceCriteria":"- Bare `ses:execution-state` resolves against current repository project and namespace.\n- Explicit qualified forms remain deterministic and unchanged.\n- If current project has no execution-state record, return project-scoped not-found rather than another project's state.\n- Add tests from at least two registered repositories with distinct execution state records.\n- Document qualified form for cross-project retrieval."}